      "location": ".claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/tools/layout.py:293",
      "judgment": "The helper requires a near-full-height narrow connected component and existing fraction baselines. It combines absolute fraction centres with strong plain-row centres, excluding nearby numerator/denominator fragments and deduplicating parallel rows. No-brace, no-fraction and fewer-than-two-row cases retain the existing estimate. The call at line641 stays inside tall-band expansion; input pixels are not edited by this helper.",
      "source_basis": "Independent p0233#7 inventory establishes two shared equation rows, not three projection slices; p0233#9 retains its real two-row wrap."
    },
    {
      "location": ".claude/skills/ld-s10y-lesson/tools/layout.py:574",
      "judgment": "The added join requires a thin fragment, a tall companion, a bounded total span and the existing single-fraction predicate. It remains subject to the common small-gap, separate-full-row and stacked-arithmetic guards. Marking a successful join in fraction_starts prevents height-only re-expansion. Neither source text nor extraction pixels are changed.",
      "source_basis": "Independent p0229#5 inventory identifies1888-1892 as the quotient identity's radical/overbar fragment, not text; p0229#3 has a genuine wrap that remains unchanged."
    }
