  "residual_risks": [
    "The narrow spanning-component check is a geometric brace proxy, not semantic brace recognition; damaged scans or unrelated thin components could trigger it. Closely spaced plain rows within1.5 glyph heights of a fraction centre may be merged. No such defect is established for the supplied affected sources.",
    "The radical join relies on the existing single-fraction predicate, not a dedicated horizontal-containment/root-component test. Very short unrelated marks near a fraction remain a heuristic risk. Existing wrapped-row, outside-row, single-fraction and stacked-arithmetic negatives pass by inherited receipts; the new file has no dedicated synthetic radical-negative case.",
    "Four historical pixel subcases were skipped. No rerun, new expected value or new corpus-wide guarantee is claimed. The focused suite is also included in the42-test fraction discovery, so suite counts must not be summed as unique cases.",
    "Existing receipts cryptographically bind commands/cwd/streams, not runtime tool or test bytes. after-binding.json matches current layout/patch, and layout/new-test mtimes precede all inherited stages; that chronology supports reuse but is not run-time cryptographic attestation. The current new-test hash is newly recorded here.",
    "Prepared layout.json files retain the original pre-repair detector evidence. Current gate counts come from the already-completed affected finalizers and audits, not from those historical layout files.",
    "p2c.py, blocks.py and the lesson SKILL.md changed concurrently after the initial evidence read. Earlier read hashes and later observed hashes are distinguished above. This review approves neither those edits nor a fresh execution of that changed finalizer stack; the scoped layout/test and affected source/receipt bindings remain unchanged.",
    "PASS is only this affected counter/source-binding review at the recorded hashes. It does not lift unrelated source holds, authorize further production, or authorize merging/publishing/closing the ticket."
  ],
